The Orb OS began as a fork of Quique Tortosa's Capsule Radar, and was called
Capsule Radar itself until August 2026. The original copyright above is
retained, as MIT requires. Substantial later work is Zion Brock's: the clock,
menu, settings, news and startup screens, the SD-card theme engine, the Orb
Studio serial and WiFi protocols, and the flash art pipeline.

The rename does not change any of the above. MIT permits modifying and
renaming, and says nothing about what a derived work may be called; what it
requires is that this notice travels with the software, which it does. The
lineage is recorded here precisely BECAUSE the name no longer carries it.

